<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balearic Islands</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Balearic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Balearic Islands are an archipelago in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menorca">Minorca</a> and Ibiza. Ibiza was a Phoenician and later Carthaginian colony, and the islands were part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>'s network. Balearic slingers were famous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> who served in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>'s armies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/balearic-islands.jpg" alt="Balearic Islands" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Balearic_Islands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
